2) Parameter Store for secrets (DB password) — ~$0

Put password in SSM Parameter Store (SecureString), e.g. /taskapp/db/password.

Change ExecStart to a tiny wrapper that fetches it at start:

# /usr/local/bin/taskapp-start.sh
DB_PASS=$(aws ssm get-parameter --name "/taskapp/db/password" --with-decryption --query Parameter.Value --output text)
exec /usr/bin/java $JAVA_OPTS -jar /opt/taskapp/backend/app.jar \
  --spring.datasource.password="$DB_PASS"


In taskapp.service:

ExecStart=/usr/local/bin/taskapp-start.sh
Environment=SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME=taskuser
Environment=SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL=jdbc:mysql://<EC2B_PRIVATE_IP>:3306/taskdb

Give EC2-A role GetParameter permission on that path.


9) DB hardening quickies — free

Create a non-root DB user (you already did).

Disable remote root login (mysql_secure_installation).

bind-address=0.0.0.0 but restrict SG to only EC2-A.

